(out/'PLAN.md').write_text(f'''# raffle.fun audit r001\n\nTarget `{f['head']}`; captured working tree was clean. User authorization is preserved in USER-AUDIT-REQUEST.txt. This is a security assessment, not production remediation or release authorization.\n\n1. Freeze tracked working-tree bytes, five production files, forge-std revision, dependency closure and all build inputs.\n2. Provide equal clean source/specification/dependencies to independent fresh contexts; omit historical findings/tests/scanner suppression.\n3. Execute 15 required harness/provider cells plus three supplementary reviews. User subsequently requested all five harnesses through a separate Daybreak Blue lane. Claude/Gemini provider-specific prompts and isolated report directories have been delivered for their own authenticated runners. Handoff is not completion.\n4. Run isolated deterministic, fuzz, invariant, static and symbolic campaigns; triage every raw scanner alert after sealing cold passes.\n5. Reconcile preserved originals by root cause, produce coverage/property matrices and unmet obligations, verify all frozen inputs.\n\nBudgets: up to 35min per OpenAI/Daybreak controller attempt; 3 targeted diagnostics per recurring setup issue, no indefinite retries. Tool commands have individual 60–600s budgets in campaign-plan.json; Echidna 100k calls/sequences per engine-reported semantics, depth 100, 180s, one worker, fixed seeds; symbolic solver budgets declared in its command. Provider handoffs have their own six-hour outer cap and 75min per cell cap. Missing stages invalidate native completion. No service purchases, broadcasts, production edits, publishing or claim of external certification.\n\nScope overrides upstream default exclusions to include interfaces. Pashov memory is off. Simao evidence is retained before cleanup. Native proof/reproduction obligations stay explicit. Trail of Bits is a declared six-stage aggregate, not the catalog. OpenKritt needs native engine and pinned workflow/resources; unavailable infrastructure remains blocked. Gebal imports are bound to exact native source/context hashes; separate test-inclusive runs may not consume cold reviews.\n\nIntegrity: python3 verify-freeze.py before/after each attempt; records stored per attempt. Source archives are hash-bound, retained read-only captures. Models are selected in the runner, fallback disabled; absent response identity stays unknown.\n''')
(out/'SCOPE.md').write_text(f'''# Scope\n\nProject raffle.fun, repository `{f['repository']}`, commit `{f['head']}`. No pre-existing working-tree changes. Core: RaffleFactory, Raffle, IRaffleFactory, IRaffle, RaffleConstants. See scope-files.txt. Five production Solidity files, 31 reachable imported dependency files. All imports, clone implementation immutables, callback base authentication, ERC721 ownership, SafeERC20 and guard behavior are part of the dependency review boundary. Versions: OpenZeppelin 5.6.1; Chainlink Contracts 1.5.0; forge-std 37a36ca389095b2f677abb07642634573ba7e265. Lockfile bytes are frozen.\n\nDeclared chain is Ethereum; Hardhat config also maintains Sepolia and local 31337. No deployed instance was supplied for scope; bytecode/live deployment comparison is NOT_APPLICABLE for this candidate. Local forks require supported RPC and explicit block; an unconfigured skipped fork is a coverage gap, not a pass. Canonical USDC and Chainlink wrapper are assumptions subject to integration checks; arbitrary prizes/receivers are untrusted.\n\nCompiler families: Foundry profiles default/ci/audit/audit_strict/audit_release share Solidity 0.8.36, Cancun, optimizer 200, viaIR=false; coverage disables optimizer; comparison enables viaIR and optimizer 1000. Capture effective configuration JSON separately for inherited/default metadata. Hardhat default and production profiles each Solidity 0.8.36, Cancun, optimizer 200. Build/test compile targets include scripts and mocks but these are not deployed production scope.\n\nAdjacent checks: SDK ABI generation/typechecks, frontend economics/transaction decisions and tests, subgraph mappings/codegen/tests, local deployment validators, lint/format, gas/size, coverage, package supply-chain. This is bounded integration validation, not a full frontend/cloud audit.\n\nExcluded from cold model contexts: tests, historical audit artifacts/reports, accepted-risk lists, scanner databases, corpora, old whitepaper archives. Full captured original bytes remain in target.tar.gz for test-inclusive deterministic runs and post-seal historical reconciliation. Clean DESIGN.md is newly derived from current README/architecture/state-machine behavior, not findings. Prior exposure: coordinator saw filenames and existing configurations/test harness source while preparing tools; cold supplementary reviewers and cell controllers received only clean contexts. Native harness resources may contain unrelated benchmark vulnerability examples.\n''')
